       It is not possible to block SSIIGGKKIILLLL or SSIIGGSSTTOOPP.  Attempts to do so  are
       silently ignored.

       Each of the threads in a process has its own signal mask.

       A  child  created  via  ffoorrkk(2)  inherits a copy of its parent’s signal
       mask; the signal mask is preserved across eexxeeccvvee(2).

       If SSIIGGBBUUSS, SSIIGGFFPPEE, SSIIGGIILLLL, or SSIIGGSSEEGGVV  are  generated  while  they  are
       blocked,  the  result  is undefined, unless the signal was generated by
       kkiillll(2), ssiiggqquueeuuee(3), or rraaiissee(3).

       See ssiiggsseettooppss(3) for details on manipulating signal sets.

       Note that it is permissible (although not very useful) to specify  both
       _s_e_t and _o_l_d_s_e_t as NULL.

